    "title": "Parole home visits lead to arrest of three on drug trafficking charges - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By A Mingo Messenger Staff Report ,\n10 hours ago Officers conducting parole compliance checks have arrested three individuals during two separate home visits, according to court documents. According to a criminal complaint, on Aug. 3, officers with the Mingo County Sheriff's Office, Gilbert Police Department and West Virginia Parole Office conducted a random parole home visit at the residence of Ashley Lea Rayburn, 44, at the Right Fork of Beech Creek in Matewan. Read full article",
